WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:10.040
Let’s look at this situation which we’d
seen in one of our earlier videos.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:14.000
Two beakers are connected by a pipe and one
of the beakers is placed at a

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.540
height above the other, and the water will
flow from this beaker to this one.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.810
Now listen to me carefully.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:24.210
If you understand this simple situation well,
you

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.880
will understand Ohm’s Law too!

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.900
Just focus for the next two minutes, and you
will master Ohm’s law!

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.730
As we’d discussed, it is the height difference
that makes the water flow from

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:39.410
the beaker on top to the one at the bottom.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:42.590
What happens if I increase the
height difference?

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:45.340
The flow of water will be faster correct?

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:46.540
Absolutely!

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:49.930
So we
can say that the FLOW of water is directly

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:51.420
proportional to the height
difference…

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.680
F α H
Now let’s look at another factor: How THIN

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.190
the pipe is!

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:59.710
What will happen if I
make the pipe thinner?

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:02.430
The flow of water will be slower right?

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:03.490
That’s correct!

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:06.159
Thinner the pipe, slower the flow!

00:01:06.159 --> 00:01:09.880
So we can say that the flow is INVERSELY
proportional to thinness.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.579
F α
Looking at these two relations, we can say

00:01:13.579 --> 00:01:16.929
that the flow is equal to H over t.

00:01:16.929 --> 00:01:19.249
F = (ignoring the constants)
The flow is directly proportional to the height

00:01:19.249 --> 00:01:22.329
difference, and inversely
proportional to the thinness.

00:01:22.329 --> 00:01:25.810
Why did I give you this example?

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:28.789
Because it’s ANALOGOUS to the Ohm’s Law.

00:01:28.789 --> 00:01:32.609
The flow of water is analogous to the flow
of CURRENT.

00:01:32.609 --> 00:01:37.399
The height difference
is analogous to the voltage or POTENTIAL DIFFERENCE!

00:01:37.399 --> 00:01:40.119
And the thinness is
analogous to the RESISTANCE.

00:01:40.119 --> 00:01:43.340
I =
The flow of current is directly proportional

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:47.530
to the potential difference between
the points and inversely proportional to the

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:49.010
resistance.

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:52.959
If the potential difference between two points
is more, the current flowing

00:01:52.959 --> 00:01:54.939
through it will be more!

00:01:54.939 --> 00:01:57.319
And if the resistance is more, the current
flowing

00:01:57.319 --> 00:01:59.680
through will be lesser!

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.509
This is assuming that the other factors are
constant.

00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:07.649
This is the basic concept of Ohm’s Law and
there are many different ways in

00:02:07.649 --> 00:02:09.229
which we can understand it.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:12.209
We will dive a bit deeper into this concept
in the

00:02:12.209 --> 00:02:15.090
coming videos!

